        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Karla Bonoff, Bonnie Raitt, Wynonna Judd, Lynn Anderson, Naomi Judd\n- Roles: Songwriters, recording artists, country music duos\n- Organizations: The Judds\n- Songs: \"Home\", \"Tell Me Why\", \"Isn't It Always Love\"\n\nFacts:\n- In the 1980s, Wynonna Judd first rose to fame alongside her mother Naomi in the country music duo The Judds.\n- As a songwriter, Karla Bonoff had songs interpreted by other artists, including Bonnie Raitt's version of \"Home.\"\n- As a songwriter, Karla Bonoff had songs interpreted by other artists, including Wynonna Judd's version of \"Tell Me Why.\"\n- As a songwriter, Karla Bonoff had songs interpreted by other artists, including Lynn Anderson's version of \"Isn't It Always Love.\"",
